. Log ticks recorded every ~10s across multiple checks confirm continuous long-running behavior.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-98e455488aa84427\",\"cmd-9c0a2b95e55e409d\",\"cmd-a98dab47bf9440d1\",\"cmd-6c3b4d95b5f04027\",\"cmd-b0c006fcd9f0499f\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Confined so the service writes only inside /var/lib/inventory\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Service unit uses ProtectSystem=strict with ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory (plus ReadOnlyPaths for the script and other hardening). Directly tested: as the service user, a write to /etc/should-fail returned Permission denied (exit=1) while a write to /var/lib/inventory/should-work succeeded (exit=0). Test artifact was removed afterward.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-98e455488aa84427\",\"cmd-6c3b4d95b5f04027\",\"cmd-9c0a2b95e55e409d\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Service gains no new privileges\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Unit sets NoNewPrivileges=yes; directly confirmed by reading /proc/<MainPID>/status on the running process, which showed NoNewPrivs: 1.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-98e455488aa84427\",\"cmd-6c3b4d95b5f04027\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol for node1 (independent of the task contract)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured (boot_id, uptime, active service, log ticks). Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection. Boot identity changed (4a74...723 -> a886...051), corroborated by fixed before_prepare/after_executor boot-identity snapshots. Post-restart recovery directly observed: service re-enabled/active with new PID, and worker.log continued appending new ticks while preserving pre-restart entries.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a98dab47bf9440d1\",\"cmd-06e3843f7d5c4e82\",\"cmd-51c6d54a7ec34885\",\"cmd-557d33e7a8984430\",\"cmd-72995ef963dd4d62\",\"cmd-5af9af3fc70b45e7\",\"cmd-2a530e688a2b4f21\",\"cmd-b0c006fcd9f0499f\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.95,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands were purposeful: user/directory creation, worker script and unit creation, service enablement, and a bounded write-confinement test whose artifact (/var/lib/inventory/should-work) was explicitly removed in the next command. The one minor residue is /tmp/reboot.log, a leftover redirect log from the backgrounded 'systemctl reboot' trigger command, which remains present in the after-executor temporary-files snapshot; it is small, non-sensitive, and a natural byproduct of the required restart-evidence step, but was not cleaned up. No failed or conflicting services, no unsafe network exposure, and no damaged package state were observed (failed-services and package-health snapshots unchanged and empty/healthy before and after).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-06e3843f7d5c4e82\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"cmd-9c0a2b95e55e409d\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor created a systemd-managed 'inventory-worker' service on node1 that runs continuously, writes only inside /var/lib/inventory (directly verified by a failed /etc write and a successful /var/lib/inventory write), and runs with NoNewPrivileges confirmed via /proc status. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also fully and directly demonstrated: healthy pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity cross-checked against fixed snapshots, and confirmed post-restart recovery of both the service and its log data. Hygiene is high with only a trivial leftover /tmp/reboot.log file.\",\"limitations\":[\"Confinement verification used the service's own MainPID and a manual sudo -u test rather than exhaustively probing every other filesystem path, so confinement outside /etc and /var/lib/inventory is inferred from the systemd sandboxing directives (ProtectSystem=strict) rather than directly tested against every location.\",\"The node-restart evidence protocol was not part of the stated task contract but was independently assessed per instructions; its strong evidence does not add to core task functionality but does raise overall confidence in node health.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Long-running background worker managed as a systemd service named inventory-worker","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unit file /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service created with ExecStart running a persistent loop script; systemctl enable --now succeeded, status shows Active: running with child sleep process; is-enabled/is-active confirm managed, enabled state. Log ticks recorded every ~10s across multiple checks confirm continuous long-running behavior.","evidence_ids":["cmd-98e455488aa84427","cmd-9c0a2b95e55e409d","cmd-a98dab47bf9440d1","cmd-6c3b4d95b5f04027","cmd-b0c006fcd9f0499f"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Confined so the service writes only inside /var/lib/inventory","status":"satisfied","summary":"Service unit uses ProtectSystem=strict with ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory (plus ReadOnlyPaths for the script and other hardening). Directly tested: as the service user, a write to /etc/should-fail returned Permission denied (exit=1) while a write to /var/lib/inventory/should-work succeeded (exit=0). Test artifact was removed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-98e455488aa84427","cmd-6c3b4d95b5f04027","cmd-9c0a2b95e55e409d"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Service gains no new privileges","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unit sets NoNewPrivileges=yes; directly confirmed by reading /proc/<MainPID>/status on the running process, which showed NoNewPrivs: 1.","evidence_ids":["cmd-98e455488aa84427","cmd-6c3b4d95b5f04027"]},{"id":"req-4","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol for node1 (independent of the task contract)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart baseline captured (boot_id, uptime, active service, log ticks). Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection. Boot identity changed (4a74...723 -> a886...051), corroborated by fixed before_prepare/after_executor boot-identity snapshots. Post-restart recovery directly observed: service re-enabled/active with new PID, and worker.log continued appending new ticks while preserving pre-restart entries.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a98dab47bf9440d1","cmd-06e3843f7d5c4e82","cmd-51c6d54a7ec34885","cmd-557d33e7a8984430","cmd-72995ef963dd4d62","cmd-5af9af3fc70b45e7","cmd-2a530e688a2b4f21","cmd-b0c006fcd9f0499f","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All state-changing commands were purposeful: user/directory creation, worker script and unit creation, service enablement, and a bounded write-confinement test whose artifact (/var/lib/inventory/should-work) was explicitly removed in the next command. The one minor residue is /tmp/reboot.log, a leftover redirect log from the backgrounded 'systemctl reboot' trigger command, which remains present in the after-executor temporary-files snapshot; it is small, non-sensitive, and a natural byproduct of the required restart-evidence step, but was not cleaned up. No failed or conflicting services, no unsafe network exposure, and no damaged package state were observed (failed-services and package-health snapshots unchanged and empty/healthy before and after).","evidence_ids":["cmd-06e3843f7d5c4e82","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","cmd-9c0a2b95e55e409d"]},"overall_summary":"The executor created a systemd-managed 'inventory-worker' service on node1 that runs continuously, writes only inside /var/lib/inventory (directly verified by a failed /etc write and a successful /var/lib/inventory write), and runs with NoNewPrivileges confirmed via /proc status. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also fully and directly demonstrated: healthy pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity cross-checked against fixed snapshots, and confirmed post-restart recovery of both the service and its log data. Hygiene is high with only a trivial leftover /tmp/reboot.log file.","limitations":["Confinement verification used the service's own MainPID and a manual sudo -u test rather than exhaustively probing every other filesystem path, so confinement outside /etc and /var/lib/inventory is inferred from the systemd sandboxing directives (ProtectSystem=strict) rather than directly tested against every location.","The node-restart evidence protocol was not part of the stated task contract but was independently assessed per instructions; its strong evidence does not add to core task functionality but does raise overall confidence in node health."]},"ttft_ms":14570,"type":"result","duration_ms":48029,"uuid":"ed797997-98b4-47f5-a1a9-77edcd5e9866","ttft_stream_ms":2355,"time_to_request_ms":186,"first_content_frame_ms":2355,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
